Subject: [PATCH 2/8] sbr_dec: run the harmonic transposer only once the stream uses it

VibeSDR patch for libxaac v0.1.14 (commit 2fbadd57; the decoder VibeServer links for xHE-AAC). Apache-2.0, as libxaac.
Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-29; applied in the order of xaac-patches/series by vibeserver/linux/build-libxaac.sh (Linux
and Mac). Every file it changes carries a "Modified by VibeSDR" notice (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). Measured with
xaacbench on the 7 ISO conformance streams, 12 xHE test streams (usac/xhe) and 4 off-air DAB+ unit logs, at PCM16 as
the server decodes, on arm64, armhf, ARMv6, i386 and amd64 (qemu) and the Mac. Instruction counts: qemu, guest
instructions per second of audio.

For AAC with eSBR (and USAC with harmonicSBR) the QMF / DFT transposer ran on every frame, though its output is read
only when the frame's sbrPatchingMode is 0. On plain HE-AAC (DAB+) it never is, and the transposer (with its cbrt()
per QMF sample, its own analysis/synthesis filterbanks) was ~30 % of the eSBR path. It now starts on the channel's
first frame with sbrPatchingMode 0 and runs on every frame after that. Output bit-identical on every test stream
(including the harmonic one). armhf DAB+ eSBR path 49.1 -> 34.4 M instr/s.
(The earlier profile's "libm pow" was this cbrt: glibc's cbrt calls frexp/ldexp, which the symbol map showed as
cbrtl/scalbnl/frexpl. SBR envelope pow() is 0.2 %, so it was left alone.)

diff --git a/decoder/ixheaacd_sbr_dec.c b/decoder/ixheaacd_sbr_dec.c
index bccc772..ab69a5d 100644
--- a/decoder/ixheaacd_sbr_dec.c
+++ b/decoder/ixheaacd_sbr_dec.c
@@ -16,6 +16,12 @@
  *
  *****************************************************************************
  * Originally developed and contributed by Ittiam Systems Pvt. Ltd, Bangalore
+ *
+ * Modified by VibeSDR, 2026-10-29: the harmonic transposer (QMF and DFT based)
+ * runs only once the stream has signalled harmonic patching (sbrPatchingMode 0)
+ * on that channel; until then its output is never read. Same output for every
+ * stream that never uses it (plain HE-AAC, DAB+), and from the first harmonic
+ * frame on it runs as before.
 */
 #include <string.h>
 #include "ixheaacd_sbr_common.h"
@@ -878,7 +884,10 @@ WORD32 ixheaacd_sbr_dec(
         ptr_sbr_dec, sbr_tables_ptr,
         op_delay + codec_x_delay + SBR_HF_ADJ_OFFSET);
 
-    if (hbe_flag && apply_processing) {
+    /* VibeSDR: the transposer only from the first frame that uses harmonic patching */
+    if (hbe_flag && apply_processing && !ptr_frame_data->sbr_patching_mode)
+      ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer->vibe_hbe_used = 1;
+    if (hbe_flag && apply_processing && ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer->vibe_hbe_used) {
       if (dft_hbe_flag == 1) {
         WORD32 err_code = 0;
         ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer->oversampling_flag =
@@ -1379,7 +1388,9 @@ WORD32 ixheaacd_esbr_dec(ia_sbr_dec_struct *ptr_sbr_dec,
       ptr_sbr_dec, ptr_sbr_tables,
       op_delay + codec_x_delay + SBR_HF_ADJ_OFFSET);
 
-  if (hbe_flag) {
+  /* VibeSDR: the transposer only from the first frame that uses harmonic patching */
+  if (hbe_flag && !ptr_frame_data->sbr_patching_mode) ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer->vibe_hbe_used = 1;
+  if (hbe_flag && ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer->vibe_hbe_used) {
     WORD32 err = ixheaacd_qmf_hbe_apply(
         ptr_sbr_dec->p_hbe_txposer,
         ptr_sbr_dec->qmf_buf_real + (op_delay + SBR_HF_ADJ_OFFSET) +
